info 7784: {"title": "Page 126", "titlalt": {}, "creato": {}, "date": {}, "dateh": {}, "callid": "mssEC 12", "physdec": {}, "placre": {}, "imprin": {}, "langua": {}, "descri": {}, "notes": "In the first telegram, the words \"not signed\" are underlined.", "notebio": {}, "locdep": {}, "subject": {}, "genre": {}, "contrib": {}, "phycola": "Thomas T. Eckert papers, 1861-1877 (bulk 1862-1867)", "phycolb": {}, "phycolc": {}, "phycold": {}, "box": {}, "folder": {}, "transc": "11.45 A. M.  Ft Monroe Va Feby 24th 1865\nFt Monroe 24th to C. C. Fulton Esq American\nOffice Balto. The U. S. Gunboat RR Cuyler\narrived this morning from Fort Fisher N. C. & brought \nthe news of the evacuation of Wilmington N. C. on the \nnight of the twenty first ---- Major Genl Terry with the Army\nentered & took possession of the city at 9 am on\nthe morning of the twenty second inst. capturing a large amount\nof supplies & stores of all kinds which the rebels\nin their haste neglected to destroy (sig) not signed ----\nMr Operator please forward the above if possible &\nwill be paid for by C. C. Fulton ----\n\n\n3 pm  New York Feby 24 1865\nN York 24th for Hon GV Fox  Asst\nSecy Navy ---- Needer is here full of\ninformation I send him to you tonight do give\nhim a full hearing I recommend that you arrange\na meeting with Grimes and other honest friends to\nhear his story tomorrow or sunday\nHS Olcott\n", "proven": {}, "bibcite": {}, "relmat": {}, "catlink": {}, "rights": "For information on use of Digital Library materials, please see Library Rights and Permissions: https://www.huntington.org/library-rights-permissions", "restri": {}, "citeas": {}, "digcol": "Thomas T. Eckert Papers, Decoding the Civil War", "digiti": "High Resolution", "datedig": "2015:10:22 11:13:48", "dcmityp": "Text", "digform": "image/jp
